AB  - The Digital Silk Road (DSR) is the component of China’s Belt and Road Initiative that aims to establish China as the global technological superpower. This chapter creates a conceptual roadmap of the DSR, which is comprised of four interrelated, technologically focused initiatives, including investment in digital infrastructure, domestic development of advanced technologies that will be essential to global economic and military power, promotion of e-commerce through digital free trade zones, and engagement in digital diplomacy and governance. Smart cities, which connect these initiatives, serve as nodes along the DSR. The chapter analyzes how the DSR will impact global governance, with a focus on the strategic technological competition between the United States and China that will shape the future international order. While the international community should welcome China’s efforts to enhance digital connectivity, there are significant risks that China will use the DSR to export its form of digital authoritarianism. © Joseph Chinyong Liow, Hong Liu and Gong Xue 2021.
