AB  - With the increasingly fierce competition among countries, the confidential work has become an important field of a country, and the image confidentiality and deciphering is one of them. If confidential work is not done well, it would easily lead to unexpected security and economic losses. We need to study more advanced technology than our competitors. Here we research the encryption algorithm of color images by combining the DNA encoding and sine chaotic mapping to encrypt the color images. Experimental results show that the speed of encryption and decryption is greatly improved because of the advantage of parallel computation; it can against a series of attacks safely and efficiently, because the algorithm has large key space, strong attack resistance, reversible encryption methods and it also sensitive to initial value. Therefore, this method is extremely suitable for the fields which collect a large amount of image data. And it also has great potential applications in the military, medicine and other image secure communication fields. © 2016 IEEE.
