AB  - As smart cities evolve with advanced surveillance systems, the balance between public safety and citizens' digital sovereignty has emerged as a critical concern. This paper presents a qualitative study that explores how modern observation techniques, such as AI-powered cameras, facial recognition, and real- time monitoring, enhance urban security while simultaneously threatening individual privacy. Through an interdisciplinary analysis of surveillance technologies, legal frameworks, and governance models, the study highlights the growing risks of mass surveillance, data misuse, and erosion of personal freedoms. The proposed framework is illustrated through the example of Delhi's smart city development, revealing systemic gaps in transparency, consent, and accountability. The paper further examines regulatory and technological strategies that can mitigate privacy invasions without undermining security goals. © 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
